    [Refactor][KV Pool] Migrate KVPOOL_RANGE_DEBUG toggle to additional_config (#19170)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    Migrate the per-layer KVPool range-debug switch from the
    `VLLM_ASCEND_KVPOOL_RANGE_DEBUG`
    environment variable to the `additional_config.kv_pool_range_debug`
    field, so it flows
    through the centralized `AscendConfig` configuration path, consistent
    with other
    switches migrated in the same way. The now-unused `_strict_binary_env`
    helper is removed.
    
    - `vllm_ascend/envs.py`: drop the `VLLM_ASCEND_KVPOOL_RANGE_DEBUG` entry
    and the `_strict_binary_env` helper.
    - `vllm_ascend/ascend_config.py`: add the typed field
    `kv_pool_range_debug: bool = False`.
    - `kv_transfer.py` and `mooncake_backend.py`: read the toggle via
    `get_ascend_config()`.
    - Docs, `zh_CN` translations and unit tests updated accordingly,
    including removal of the
    now-obsolete negative test
    `test_kvpool_range_debug_is_not_an_environment_setting`.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    Yes. The debug switch is now set through `additional_config` instead of
    an environment
    variable. The default stays disabled (`false`) and runtime behavior is
    unchanged when the
    option is not configured.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    - `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` pass for all changed Python
    files (the repo-pinned
    ruff is v0.14.0; local check used v0.16.10, and the only reported
    reformat target is a
      pre-existing line unrelated to this change).
    - Unit tests updated: `tests/ut/test_ascend_config.py`,
    `tests/ut/test_envs.py`,
      `tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store/test_mooncake_layerwise.py`.
    - Full unit tests / NPU and end-to-end validation are expected to run in
    CI.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: weijinqian0 <1184188277@qq.com>

